Note: Flatten Procedure will be covered in next session.
  
KEY COMPONENTS:
 
1. ORCHESTRATOR DAG (MAXI_RAW_ORCHESTRATOR_DAG)
   - Runs hourly, reads config from S3 (MAXIMUS_RAW_MASTER.json)
   - Groups tables by sync type: FRO (Full Refresh) or INU (Incremental)
   - Triggers child DAGs: MAXI_RAW_S3_TO_SF_FRO or MAXI_RAW_S3_TO_SF_INU
 
2. CONFIGURATION MANAGEMENT
   - Master config managed via Snowflake stored procedure (no manual editing)
   - Auto-syncs to S3 hourly; manual trigger available for immediate sync
   - Maintains change logs and timestamped backups
 
3. DATA FLOW (Per Table)
   a. Get previous state from MAXI_RAW_STATE_TABLE
   b. Scan S3 for new files, batch them (FRO: 999, INU: 999 files/batch)
   c. Load to staging table via SNOWFLAKE_COPY_INA_STAGING_JOB_MAXI_RAW
   d. Call WRAPPER_PROC to flatten json data (creates mirror tables)
   e. Update state table with max file timestamp of json files
 
4. RECOVERY MECHANISM
   - CHECKPOINT_TABLE tracks batch-level progress
   - On failure, job resumes from last successful batch
 
5. SCHEMA DRIFT DETECTION
   - Metadata procedure compares incremental vs. old metadata tables
   - New columns: Auto-added to metadata
   - Type changes: Job FAILS intentionally for team review
   - After review, drift correction procedure can be applied
 
 
